<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Juan de Garay</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1528–1583</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Juan de Garay was a Basque-born conquistador who served in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peru">Peru</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paraguay">Paraguay</a>. From <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asuncion">Asunción</a> he founded Santa Fe in 1573 and refounded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buenos-aires">Buenos Aires</a> in 1580, decades after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pedro-de-mendoza">Pedro de Mendoza</a>'s first settlement had been abandoned. As governor in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rio-de-la-plata">Río de la Plata</a> he distributed land and native labour, and he was killed by indigenous warriors in 1583.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/juan-de-garay.jpg" alt="Juan de Garay" width="318" height="454" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Garay.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
